{
  "version": "2.1",
  "meta": {
    "title": "Backpropagation on a tiny network",
    "summary": "One full training step on a 2-2-1 network: forward pass, loss, every gradient via the chain rule, the weight update, and a second forward pass that proves the loss dropped."
  },
  "layout": {
    "direction": "LR",
    "edges": "straight"
  },
  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "input",
      "label": "Input"
    },
    {
      "id": "hidden",
      "label": "Hidden"
    },
    {
      "id": "output",
      "label": "Output"
    }
  ],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "x1",
      "label": "x1 = 1.0",
      "kind": "value",
      "group": "input"
    },
    {
      "id": "x2",
      "label": "x2 = 0.5",
      "kind": "value",
      "group": "input"
    },
    {
      "id": "h1",
      "label": "h1",
      "kind": "value",
      "group": "hidden"
    },
    {
      "id": "h2",
      "label": "h2",
      "kind": "value",
      "group": "hidden"
    },
    {
      "id": "y",
      "label": "y",
      "kind": "value",
      "group": "output"
    },
    {
      "id": "loss",
      "label": "L",
      "kind": "value"
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "id": "w1",
      "from": "x1",
      "to": "h1",
      "label": "w1"
    },
    {
      "id": "w2",
      "from": "x2",
      "to": "h1",
      "label": "w2"
    },
    {
      "id": "w3",
      "from": "x1",
      "to": "h2",
      "label": "w3"
    },
    {
      "id": "w4",
      "from": "x2",
      "to": "h2",
      "label": "w4"
    },
    {
      "id": "w5",
      "from": "h1",
      "to": "y",
      "label": "w5"
    },
    {
      "id": "w6",
      "from": "h2",
      "to": "y",
      "label": "w6"
    },
    {
      "id": "sq",
      "from": "y",
      "to": "loss",
      "label": "(t−y)²"
    }
  ],
  "arrays": [
    {
      "id": "weights",
      "label": "Weights",
      "values": [
        "0.4",
        "0.2",
        "0.3",
        "0.6",
        "0.7",
        "0.5"
      ],
      "keys": [
        "w1",
        "w2",
        "w3",
        "w4",
        "w5",
        "w6"
      ],
      "pos": {
        "x": 240,
        "y": 260
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grads",
      "label": "Gradients dL/dw",
      "values": [
        "–",
        "–",
        "–",
        "–",
        "–",
        "–"
      ],
      "keys": [
        "w1",
        "w2",
        "w3",
        "w4",
        "w5",
        "w6"
      ],
      "pos": {
        "x": 240,
        "y": 390
      }
    }
  ],
  "code": [
    {
      "id": "src",
      "title": "Training step (pseudo-code)",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "# forward\nh1 = w1*x1 + w2*x2\nh2 = w3*x1 + w4*x2\ny  = w5*h1 + w6*h2\nL  = (t - y) ** 2\n# backward (chain rule)\ndy = 2 * (y - t)\ndw5, dw6 = dy*h1, dy*h2\ndh1, dh2 = dy*w5, dy*w6\ndw1, dw2 = dh1*x1, dh1*x2\ndw3, dw4 = dh2*x1, dh2*x2\n# update\nw -= lr * dw   # every weight",
      "pos": {
        "x": 690,
        "y": 260
      }
    }
  ],
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "id": "train",
      "title": "One training step",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "setup",
          "title": "The tiny network",
          "narration": "Two inputs (x1 = 1.0, x2 = 0.5), two hidden neurons, one output, six weights w1–w6. Target t = 1.0, learning rate lr = 0.1. To keep the arithmetic readable there is no activation function, every neuron is just a weighted sum. Goal: nudge the weights so y moves toward 1.0.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "callout",
              "target": "y",
              "text": "Target t = 1.0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "fwd-h1",
          "title": "Forward: h1",
          "narration": "h1 = w1·x1 + w2·x2 = 0.4·1.0 + 0.2·0.5 = 0.4 + 0.1 = **0.5**. Each weight scales the value on its edge and the neuron adds them up.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "2"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "x1",
              "to": "h1",
              "label": "0.4"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "x2",
              "to": "h1",
              "label": "0.1",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "h1",
              "text": "h1 = 0.5"
            },
            {
              "do": "state",
              "targets": [
                "h1"
              ],
              "state": "active"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "fwd-h2",
          "title": "Forward: h2",
          "narration": "h2 = w3·x1 + w4·x2 = 0.3·1.0 + 0.6·0.5 = 0.3 + 0.3 = **0.6**. Same inputs, different weights, so a different value.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "3"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "x1",
              "to": "h2",
              "label": "0.3"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "x2",
              "to": "h2",
              "label": "0.3",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "h2",
              "text": "h2 = 0.6"
            },
            {
              "do": "state",
              "targets": [
                "h2"
              ],
              "state": "active"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "fwd-out",
          "title": "Forward: output",
          "narration": "y = w5·h1 + w6·h2 = 0.7·0.5 + 0.5·0.6 = 0.35 + 0.30 = **0.65**. The network predicts 0.65 but the target is 1.0.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "4"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "h1",
              "to": "y",
              "label": "0.35"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "h2",
              "to": "y",
              "label": "0.30",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "y",
              "text": "y = 0.65"
            },
            {
              "do": "state",
              "targets": [
                "y"
              ],
              "state": "warning"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "loss",
          "title": "Loss and its first gradient",
          "narration": "Loss L = (t − y)² = (1.0 − 0.65)² = 0.35² = **0.1225**. Backprop starts here: dL/dy = 2(y − t) = 2·(0.65 − 1.0) = **−0.70**. Negative means raising y lowers the loss.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "5,7"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "y",
              "to": "loss",
              "label": "0.1225"
            },
            {
              "do": "state",
              "targets": [
                "y",
                "loss"
              ],
              "state": "error"
            },
            {
              "do": "callout",
              "target": "loss",
              "text": "L = 0.1225"
            },
            {
              "do": "callout",
              "target": "y",
              "text": "dL/dy = −0.70"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "back-out",
          "title": "Gradients of the output weights",
          "narration": "A weight's gradient = (gradient arriving at its output) × (the input it multiplied). dL/dw5 = dy·h1 = −0.70·0.5 = **−0.35**. dL/dw6 = dy·h2 = −0.70·0.6 = **−0.42**.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "8"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "loss",
              "to": "y",
              "label": "−0.70"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "y",
              "to": "h1",
              "label": "−0.35",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "y",
              "to": "h2",
              "label": "−0.42",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "grads#w5",
              "text": "−0.35"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "grads#w6",
              "text": "−0.42",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "state",
              "targets": [
                "h1",
                "h2"
              ],
              "state": "warning"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "back-hidden",
          "title": "Pass the error to the hidden layer",
          "narration": "To go further back, ask how much each hidden value affected y. dL/dh1 = dy·w5 = −0.70·0.7 = **−0.49**, dL/dh2 = dy·w6 = −0.70·0.5 = **−0.35**. Note: this uses the old w5 and w6, before any update.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "9"
            },
            {
              "do": "callout",
              "target": "h1",
              "text": "dL/dh1 = −0.49"
            },
            {
              "do": "callout",
              "target": "h2",
              "text": "dL/dh2 = −0.35"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "back-h1",
          "title": "Gradients into h1",
          "narration": "h1 was fed by x1 and x2 through w1 and w2. dL/dw1 = dh1·x1 = −0.49·1.0 = **−0.49**. dL/dw2 = dh1·x2 = −0.49·0.5 = **−0.245**.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "10"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "h1",
              "to": "x1",
              "label": "−0.49"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "h1",
              "to": "x2",
              "label": "−0.245",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "grads#w1",
              "text": "−0.49"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "grads#w2",
              "text": "−0.245",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "state",
              "targets": [
                "x1",
                "x2"
              ],
              "state": "warning"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "back-h2",
          "title": "Gradients into h2",
          "narration": "Same for h2: dL/dw3 = dh2·x1 = −0.35·1.0 = **−0.35**. dL/dw4 = dh2·x2 = −0.35·0.5 = **−0.175**. Now all six weights have a gradient, and they are all negative: each weight should increase.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "11"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "h2",
              "to": "x1",
              "label": "−0.35"
            },
            {
              "do": "send",
              "from": "h2",
              "to": "x2",
              "label": "−0.175",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "grads#w3",
              "text": "−0.35"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "grads#w4",
              "text": "−0.175",
              "start": "with"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "update",
          "title": "Update every weight",
          "narration": "Gradient descent: w ← w − lr·grad, with lr = 0.1. w1: 0.4 + 0.049 = **0.449**; w2: 0.2 + 0.0245 = **0.2245**; w3: 0.3 + 0.035 = **0.335**; w4: 0.6 + 0.0175 = **0.6175**; w5: 0.7 + 0.035 = **0.735**; w6: 0.5 + 0.042 = **0.542**.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "13"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w1",
              "text": "0.449"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w2",
              "text": "0.2245",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w3",
              "text": "0.335",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w4",
              "text": "0.6175",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w5",
              "text": "0.735",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w6",
              "text": "0.542",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "state",
              "targets": [
                "x1",
                "x2",
                "h1",
                "h2",
                "y",
                "loss"
              ],
              "state": "success"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "recheck",
          "title": "Did it work? Forward again",
          "narration": "With the new weights: h1 = 0.449·1.0 + 0.2245·0.5 = 0.5613, h2 = 0.335 + 0.6175·0.5 = 0.6438, y = 0.735·0.5613 + 0.542·0.6438 = **0.7614**. Loss = (1 − 0.7614)² = **0.0569**, down from 0.1225. Repeat many times and y converges to 1.0.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "2-5"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "h1",
              "text": "h1 = 0.56"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "h2",
              "text": "h2 = 0.64",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "y",
              "text": "y = 0.76",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "callout",
              "target": "loss",
              "text": "0.1225 → 0.0569"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lr-too-high",
      "title": "What if the learning rate is too high?",
      "branchFrom": {
        "scenario": "train",
        "afterStep": "back-h2"
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "big-update",
          "title": "Update with lr = 5",
          "narration": "Same gradients, but lr = 5. w1: 0.4 + 2.45 = **2.85**; w2: 0.2 + 1.225 = **1.425**; w3: 0.3 + 1.75 = **2.05**; w4: 0.6 + 0.875 = **1.475**; w5: 0.7 + 1.75 = **2.45**; w6: 0.5 + 2.1 = **2.6**. Each step is 50× bigger than before.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "13"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w1",
              "text": "2.85"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w2",
              "text": "1.425",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w3",
              "text": "2.05",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w4",
              "text": "1.475",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w5",
              "text": "2.45",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "weights#w6",
              "text": "2.6",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "state",
              "targets": [
                "y",
                "loss"
              ],
              "state": "error"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "big-forward",
          "title": "Overshoot: the loss explodes",
          "narration": "Forward again: h1 = 2.85 + 1.425·0.5 = 3.5625, h2 = 2.05 + 1.475·0.5 = 2.7875, y = 2.45·3.5625 + 2.6·2.7875 = **15.98**. Loss = (1 − 15.98)² ≈ **224**, about 1800× worse. The gradient only says which way to go, lr decides how far.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "highlight",
              "target": "src",
              "lines": "2-5"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "h1",
              "text": "h1 = 3.56"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "h2",
              "text": "h2 = 2.79",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "label",
              "target": "y",
              "text": "y = 15.98",
              "start": "with"
            },
            {
              "do": "callout",
              "target": "loss",
              "text": "Diverges: 0.1225 → 224"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}